{% comment %}
TRMNL renders Liquid in UTC, so shift into the user's zone before comparing against
the London local times National Rail returns. `visible_count` counts services that
have not departed yet at render time; the size templates skip the rest. Those left
before this screen existed, so dropping them can never hide a train you could still
have caught.

A service is judged on when it will actually leave, not when it was scheduled to:
  etd is a time ("14:14")  -> use it, so a delayed train survives past its std
  etd is "Delayed"         -> no estimate given, it has not left, always keep
  etd is "On time"         -> use std
  etd is "Cancelled"       -> use std, so it drops once its slot passes
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign now_local = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | plus: trmnl.user.utc_offset -%}
{%- assign today_local = now_local | date: "%d %B %Y " -%}
{%- assign visible_count = 0 -%}
{%- for service in trainServices -%}
{%- assign eff = service.std -%}
{%- assign eff_unknown = false -%}
{%- if service.etd contains ":" -%}{%- assign eff = service.etd -%}
{%- elsif service.etd == "Delayed" -%}{%- assign eff_unknown = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign eff_local = today_local | append: eff | date: "%s" -%}
{%- assign eff_delta = eff_local | minus: now_local -%}
{%- if eff_delta < -21600 -%}{%- assign eff_delta = eff_delta | plus: 86400 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if eff_delta >= 0 or eff_unknown -%}{%- assign visible_count = visible_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}